---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Who We Serve" description="IONIC serves SACCOs, microfinance institutions, manufacturers, distributors, multi-branch retailers, and NGOs across East Africa.">

  <section class="page-hero section-dark">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label" style="color:var(--cyan);">Our Clients</p>
      <h1 style="color:var(--white); max-width:640px;">Built for organizations where data complexity is a daily reality.</h1>
      <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.75); max-width:560px; margin-top:16px; font-size:1.05rem;">
        IONIC's solutions are most compelling where three conditions exist: transaction volume, regulatory pressure, and financial complexity. Here is who we serve.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PRIMARY -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container tier-block">
      <div class="tier-label">
        <span class="tier-badge primary">Primary</span>
        <p class="tier-retainer">KSh 30,000 – 60,000 / month</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-body">
        <h2>Financially-Structured Organizations</h2>
        <p style="font-size:1.05rem; margin-bottom:24px;">SACCOs, microfinance institutions, small lending institutions, and financial cooperatives. This is IONIC's highest-value target segment.</p>
        <div class="why-grid">
          <div class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon">📋</div>
            <h3>Data-heavy by necessity</h3>
            <p>They track loans, repayments, member accounts, and defaults every single day. The data is there — it just needs to be turned into intelligence.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon">⚖️</div>
            <h3>Regulatory reporting obligations</h3>
            <p>SASRA, CBK, and other regulatory bodies require structured, accurate, regular reporting. IONIC automates these submissions.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon">💡</div>
            <h3>Already data-literate</h3>
            <p>These organizations understand dashboards and are primed to see value quickly. The sales cycle is shorter because the problem is well understood.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon">💰</div>
            <h3>Budget for sustained engagement</h3>
            <p>Sufficient monthly cash flow to sustain a retainer relationship. They invest in operations tools because the ROI is clear and measurable.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tier-types">
          <span class="tag tag-dark">SACCOs</span>
          <span class="tag tag-dark">Microfinance Institutions</span>
          <span class="tag tag-dark">Lending Cooperatives</span>
          <span class="tag tag-dark">Financial Cooperatives</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECONDARY -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container tier-block">
      <div class="tier-label">
        <span class="tier-badge secondary">Secondary</span>
        <p class="tier-retainer">KSh 25,000 – 50,000 / month</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-body">
        <h2>Operational SMEs</h2>
        <p style="font-size:1.05rem; margin-bottom:24px;">Manufacturing companies, distribution businesses, multi-branch retail, and agribusiness. These organizations generate rich operational data but manage it in disconnected spreadsheets.</p>
        <div class="why-grid">
          <div class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon">📦</div>
            <h3>Inventory leakage</h3>
            <p>Stock discrepancies and procurement inefficiencies are high-cost problems that dashboards and predictive models catch and eliminate.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon">📈</div>
            <h3>Sales vs. target tracking</h3>
            <p>Sales figures are recorded manually and compared against targets in spreadsheets. IONIC replaces this with a live performance dashboard.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon">🏪</div>
            <h3>Branch performance</h3>
            <p>Multi-branch operations need consolidation. IONIC automates the comparison of branch-level performance on a single screen.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon">🔄</div>
            <h3>Production planning</h3>
            <p>Predictive models add measurable value to procurement and production cycles — reducing overstock, understock, and waste.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tier-types">
          <span class="tag tag-dark">Manufacturing</span>
          <span class="tag tag-dark">Distribution</span>
          <span class="tag tag-dark">Multi-Branch Retail</span>
          <span class="tag tag-dark">Agribusiness</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TERTIARY -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container tier-block">
      <div class="tier-label">
        <span class="tier-badge tertiary">Tertiary</span>
        <p class="tier-retainer">KSh 15,000 – 30,000 / month</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-body">
        <h2>NGOs & Development Organizations</h2>
        <p style="font-size:1.05rem; margin-bottom:24px;">Grant-funded NGOs, development organizations, and community programs with field data. Pursued selectively — they are strong credibility builders and generate referrals within the development sector.</p>
        <div class="why-grid">
          <div class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon">📝</div>
            <h3>Donor reporting</h3>
            <p>Structured, visual data outputs are exactly what donors expect. IONIC produces these automatically from field and program data.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon">🗣</div>
            <h3>Survey & feedback analysis</h3>
            <p>Weeks of manual open-response analysis reduced to hours using AI. Critical for impact reports and program evaluations.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon">🗺</div>
            <h3>Location-based monitoring</h3>
            <p>Regional program performance mapped and compared spatially. Ideal for NGOs running multi-county or multi-country programs.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon">🤝</div>
            <h3>Referral network</h3>
            <p>Well-networked NGOs refer IONIC to the more data-mature organizations they work with — banks, government bodies, and large SMEs.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tier-types">
          <span class="tag tag-dark">Grant-Funded NGOs</span>
          <span class="tag tag-dark">Development Organizations</span>
          <span class="tag tag-dark">Field Programs</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- QUALIFICATION FILTER -->
  <section class="section section-dark">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:700px; text-align:center;">
      <p class="section-label" style="color:var(--cyan);">Qualification Filter</p>
      <h2 style="color:var(--white); margin-bottom:24px;">Is IONIC right for your organization?</h2>
      <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.75); margin-bottom:40px;">IONIC's solutions deliver the most value where at least two of these three conditions are present:</p>
      <div class="filter-grid">
        <div class="filter-item">
          <span class="filter-num">1</span>
          <h3 style="color:var(--white);">Transaction Volume</h3>
          <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);">Enough data flowing through the business daily to make dashboards and automation genuinely valuable.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="filter-item">
          <span class="filter-num">2</span>
          <h3 style="color:var(--white);">Regulatory Pressure</h3>
          <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);">External reporting requirements that create recurring, ongoing analytics demand.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="filter-item">
          <span class="filter-num">3</span>
          <h3 style="color:var(--white);">Financial Complexity</h3>
          <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);">Multiple revenue streams, cost centers, loan portfolios, or branches to track and reconcile.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-white" style="margin-top:40px;">Talk to Us About Your Organization</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
.page-hero { padding: 80px 0 72px; }
.tier-block { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr; gap: 48px; align-items: start; }
.tier-label { text-align: center; padding-top: 8px; }
.tier-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 6px 18px; border-radius: 99px; font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
.tier-badge.primary   { background: var(--teal-dark); color: var(--cyan); }
.tier-badge.secondary { background: var(--teal-mid); color: var(--white); }
.tier-badge.tertiary  { background: var(--gray-light); color: var(--gray-text); }
.tier-retainer { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--gray-mid); font-weight: 600; }
.tier-body h2 { color: var(--teal-dark); margin-bottom: 12px; }
.why-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
.why-item { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid #E5E7EB; border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: 20px; }
.why-icon { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 10px; }
.why-item h3 { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--teal-dark); margin-bottom: 6px; }
.why-item p { font-size: 0.87rem; }
.tier-types { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-top: 20px; }
.filter-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 24px; text-align: left; }
.filter-item { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.06); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: 24px; }
.filter-num { display: block; font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--cyan); margin-bottom: 12px; }
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .tier-block { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
  .why-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .filter-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}
</style>
